SUMMARY:Mission of Gravity - Hal Clement
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi everybody\,\n\nBack for another team 
 investigating an alien planet. This time we have a true classic\, Hal Clem
 ent's seminal 1954 gritty sci fi novel\, *Missions of Gravity*. This one h
 as been on the list for a while and I'm so glad it was on theme enough to 
 get on the survey.\n\nBook of the Month\n*Mission of Gravity* \\- Hal Clem
 ent \\(1954\\)\n\nFrom a good review on Skiffy.ca\, "Originally serialized
  in 1953 in the magazine *[Astounding Science Fiction](https://en.wikipedi
 a.org/wiki/Analog_Science_Fiction_and_Fact)*\, the tale was published in b
 ook form the following year. Decades later\, it was awarded a [Retro Hugo]
 (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugo_Award#Retro_Hugos)\, for excellence in
  SF’s pioneering era.\n\n*Mission of Gravity* is an archetypal example o
 f what the kids call “hard science fiction”\, a subgenre in which the 
 characters within the SF story solve physical problems with physical –la
 rgely technological– means. The science tends to be solid\, even the spe
 culative science\, and the rules are intensely consistent within the bound
 aries of the story."\n\nTo join a Book Club meeting\, all you will need is
  YOURSELF. If you haven’t had a chance to finish the book\, we still wou
 ld love for you to join us in the discussion.\n\nNot able to join us in pe
 rson for events? [The Sci Fi Book Club is on Discord](https://discord.gg/B
 9NMnC2F). Join us and keep the conversation going.
